# .kilocodeignore — files Kilo Code should not access or index.
# Standard .gitignore syntax. Patterns are relative to the repo root.
#
# Purpose: the semantic-search index was being flooded by huge generated/data
# files (loader manifests, lock files, generated Tauri schemas, audit-log
# archives), so agent searches on any Minecraft-domain query returned only
# noise. Listing those files here drops them from the index.
#
# TRADEOFF: a path listed here becomes UNREADABLE and UNEDITABLE by agents
# (IgnoreMigrator turns these into read/edit deny rules). If an agent needs a
# listed file — most notably the two loader-manifest JSONs during loader
# curation — temporarily comment that line out for that session.

# --- Build output, dependencies, caches (carried over from .gitignore) -----
.venv
node_modules
target
dist
.next
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
.DS_Store
__pycache__
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
playwright-report/
test-results/
local_state.db
registry.db
registry.db.sig
*.db
*.db.sig
tokens.enc
.cache
.pnpm-store
.idea

# --- Local caches / editor / CI dirs (not source) --------------------------
.pytest_cache
.codex-kilo
.vscode

# --- Large generated data that drowns out real code in semantic search ----

# Loader manifest bulk data: tens of thousands of installer URLs + hash lists.
# NOTE: deny edit here blocks loader curation — comment out when pinning a
# new loader version, then re-enable.
loader-manifests/loader_manifests.json
loader-manifests/known_good_hashes.json

# Generated Tauri capability/schema JSON (build output, never hand-edited).
desktop/src-tauri/gen/

# Governance audit logs (live + archived — repetitive entries drown crash queries).
registry/governance/audit_log.json
registry/governance/audit_log_archive.*.json

# Runtime hash catalog — dense SHA-256 list that pollutes short generic queries.
runtime-catalog/runtime_catalog.json

# --- Dependency lock files (no semantic value; agents should grep, not read) 
*.lock
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
yarn.lock
bun.lock

# --- Native build artifacts / binaries (never source; some are hundreds of MB)
*.pdb
*.rlib
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.lib
*.a
*.o